ntdll virtual memory on wasm64: write-watch, queries, KUSER and pointer
validation (docs/design/wine-unix.md, sections 4 and 6).

- PAGE_WATCH in the page-state table follows VPROT_WRITEWATCH: set_page_vprot,
  set_page_vprot_bits and set_page_vprot_exec_write_protect tell the backend
  (tw_page_watch), since translated code checks writes against the table.
- NtQueryVirtualMemory reports what lies outside the guest regions (the NULL
  region, the gap, the host region) as reserved, as Wine does on i386
  outside its reserved areas; a free region ends where the guest regions do.
- KUSER is one page: virtual_map_user_shared_data maps nothing, and
  virtual_init_user_shared_data writes 0x7ffe0000 in place, with no USD
  section.
- A bad guest pointer doesn't fault, so the three __TRY sites
  (virtual_check_buffer_for_read, virtual_check_buffer_for_write and
  NtReadVirtualMemory) check the pages against the views instead.

